            <ArticleTitle>Unexpected coronary vasospasm of a contralateral artery during balloon angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>82-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is unusual for coronary vasospasm to develop following angioplasty of a coronary vascular lesion that is located elsewhere. We experienced a rare case of shock with vasospasm of the right coronary artery in a patient following balloon angioplasty performed for stent restenosis of the left anterior descending artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
